      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: a cost event was created 75 minutes after Pending Close\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine–DeKoven operation.\n\n| Item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` |\n| Source transaction | `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` |\n| Event type | `INPUT` — “Component issue after pending close” |\n| Amount | **USD $284,763.42** (`28,476,342` cents) |\n| Exact event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| Exact September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 4,500 seconds ÷ 60 |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\nThe timestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source supplies no time-zone offset.\n\n### Policy conclusion\n\nThe recorded **`POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment** for this event type and timing.\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** (PDF page **233**, printed page **225**), states that transactions created after Pending Close—even for the current or a prior period—will not be processed until the period is closed or reopened. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions, but this event is an **INPUT component issue**, not one of those exceptions.\n\n**Evidence and review status:** The work-order, period, and policy records were read directly. Because the assigned supporting input was not staged, the event details were obtained from an authorized analyst’s verified work product and checked against its service-generated source-read receipt. The audit was saved to `/cache/work/worker_13914e6bea46/audit-report.json` and submitted; automated evidence validation remains incomplete.\n\n**No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
